{"id":31036,"slug":"rolling-thunder-revue-a-bob-dylan-story-by-martin-scorsese","title":"Rolling Thunder Revue: A Bob Dylan Story by Martin Scorsese","year":2019,"country":"United States","duration":142,"spine":1062,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/31036-rolling-thunder-revue-a-bob-dylan-story-by-martin-scorsese","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/859cb0d19e424453f8d3634b401bb8c3/XyQ5pkrk4GrUByTTdbK4LQRskAytRF_large.jpg","description":"In 1975, in an America defined by both the self-mythologizing pomp of the upcoming bicentennial and ongoing sociopolitical turmoil, Bob Dylan and a band of troubadours—including luminaries such as Joan Baez, Allen Ginsberg, and Joni Mitchell—embarked on a now-legendary tour known as the Rolling Thunder Revue, a freewheeling variety show that was part traveling counterculture carnival, part spiritual pilgrimage. Director Martin Scorsese blends behind-the-scenes archival footage, interviews, and narrative mischief, with a magician’s sleight of hand, into a zeitgeist-defining cultural record that is as much a concert “documentary” as it is a slippery, chimerical investigation into memory, time, truth, and illusion. At the center of it all is the magnetic Dylan, a sphinxlike philosopher-poet singing, with electrifying conviction, to the soul of an anxious nation.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Martin Scorsese","slug":"martin-scorsese"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Bob Dylan","role":"Himself","slug":"bob-dylan"},{"actor":"Allen Ginsberg","role":"The Oracle of Delphi","slug":"allen-ginsberg"},{"actor":"Patti Smith","role":"The Punk Poet","slug":"patti-smith"},{"actor":"Martin von Haselberg","role":"The Filmmaker","slug":"martin-von-haselberg"},{"actor":"Scarlet Rivera","role":"The Queen of Swords","slug":"scarlet-rivera"},{"actor":"Joan Baez","role":"The Balladeer","slug":"joan-baez"},{"actor":"Roger McGuinn","role":"The Minstrel","slug":"roger-mcguinn"},{"actor":"Larry “Ratso” Sloman","role":"The Rollin